  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 111 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nFrom Monday int late week, the region will dry out as drier mid \nlevel west-northwesterly flow develops over the region. It should be \nnoted it will be much cooler this week, with mainly 60s over \nthe plains for max temps and 50s in the valleys. \n\nBy next weekend, another surge of moisture will move in from the \nPacific and move across the intermountain west, bringing the \npotential for more precipitation to the high terrain. At this \ntime the deterministic GFS is much more bullish then the EC with\nregard to this system. The statistical guidance products start \nto show precip developing (mainly snow), especially over the \nmtns, by next weekend.",
